  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "In quadrilateral \\(ABCD\\), \\(\\angle C=\\angle D=90^\\circ\\), \\(AC=BD=8\\), and \\(BC=6\\). Find the length of \\(AD\\).",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "6",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "In right triangles \\(ADC\\) and \\(BCD\\), the hypotenuses satisfy \\(AC=BD=8\\), and \\(DC\\) is a common leg. The triangles are congruent by HL, so \\(AD=BC=6\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: Compare Pythagorean equations\n\nThe right angles at \\(D\\) and \\(C\\) let us apply the Pythagorean theorem to \\(\\triangle ADC\\) and \\(\\triangle BCD\\). Their equal hypotenuses and common leg \\(CD\\) give\n\\[\nAD^2=AC^2-CD^2=BD^2-CD^2=BC^2=6^2=36.\n\\]\nBecause \\(AD\\) is a positive length, \\(AD=6\\).",
